WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.205
Let's make A tiny twig sailboat.

2
00:00:02.585 --> 00:00:06.478
Tie five or six short twigs into a miniature raft, add a leaf sail

3
00:00:06.478 --> 00:00:08.425
and test it in a shallow tray.

4
00:00:08.805 --> 00:00:11.915
Retrieve the boat and all materials after play.

5
00:00:12.295 --> 00:00:14.375
Make this project with a grown-up.

6
00:00:14.755 --> 00:00:17.485
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

7
00:00:17.865 --> 00:00:20.110
Pause whenever you need more time.

8
00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:25.348
An adult handles tight knots, checks twig ends and stays beside the shallow water

9
00:00:25.348 --> 00:00:25.695
tray.

10
00:00:26.075 --> 00:00:29.355
No streams, ponds or open-water launching.

11
00:00:29.735 --> 00:00:32.095
The sail is decorative and may tip the raft.

12
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.690
Step 1.

13
00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.715
Line up the raft twigs.

14
00:00:37.095 --> 00:00:41.620
Place five or six similar twigs side by side with their ends level.

15
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.250
Leave a tiny gap between each.

16
00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:47.135
Set aside the shorter mast twig and leaf.

17
00:00:47.515 --> 00:00:48.895
Grown-up help.

18
00:00:49.275 --> 00:00:51.130
Prepare smooth twig lengths.

19
00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:53.847
Step 2.

20
00:00:54.227 --> 00:00:55.907
Lash the first end.

21
00:00:56.287 --> 00:01:00.893
About 2 centimetres from one end, an adult ties a string around the first

22
00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:01.222
twig.

23
00:01:01.602 --> 00:01:05.687
Weave it over and under the next twigs, then back along the row.

24
00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.527
Pull snug and knot to the starting end.

25
00:01:08.907 --> 00:01:10.287
Grown-up help.

26
00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:13.017
Tie the starting and finishing knots.

27
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.845
Step 3.

28
00:01:16.225 --> 00:01:17.855
Secure the other end.

29
00:01:18.235 --> 00:01:22.460
Repeat with the second long string about 2 centimetres from the opposite end.

30
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:26.885
Check that all the twigs stay together when the raft is gently lifted.

31
00:01:27.265 --> 00:01:29.800
Trim trailing string only by an adult.

32
00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.560
Grown-up help.

33
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.835
Tie and trim the string ends.

34
00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:36.484
Step 4.

35
00:01:36.864 --> 00:01:38.519
Add a small sail.

36
00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:41.419
Push the mast into the middle gap in the raft.

37
00:01:41.799 --> 00:01:45.229
Use the short string to tie it to a middle twig at the base.

38
00:01:45.609 --> 00:01:49.244
Fold the leaf stem around the mast and tuck it into the same tie.

39
00:01:49.624 --> 00:01:51.119
Keep the sail low.

40
00:01:51.499 --> 00:01:52.879
Grown-up help.

41
00:01:53.259 --> 00:01:57.079
Secure the mast; leave the sail off if it will not balance.

42
00:01:58.501 --> 00:01:59.676
Step 5.

43
00:02:00.056 --> 00:02:02.171
Float, adjust, retrieve.

44
00:02:02.551 --> 00:02:06.391
Set the raft gently in the tray with 2 to 3 centimetres of water.

45
00:02:06.771 --> 00:02:10.066
If it tips, remove the sail and try the plain raft.

46
00:02:10.446 --> 00:02:14.711
Lift it out afterward, empty the tray and collect every string and twig.

47
00:02:15.091 --> 00:02:16.471
Grown-up help.

48
00:02:16.851 --> 00:02:19.481
Stay beside the tray and empty it after use.

49
00:02:21.001 --> 00:02:23.916
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

50
00:02:24.296 --> 00:02:27.846
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

51
00:02:28.226 --> 00:02:30.246
Your creation can look different.

52
00:02:30.626 --> 00:02:34.611
Untie and reuse string, dry the tray and sort natural pieces.

53
00:02:34.991 --> 00:02:40.341
Dry the pieces separately before storing; wet string and leaves should not stay bundled.

54
00:02:40.721 --> 00:02:41.711
Well done.

55
00:02:42.091 --> 00:02:44.521
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

